id:                     E452
trigger_tool: conan|binary-sign-tool|llvm-objcopy|dynamic-loader
phase: testing|runtime|package-consumer
error_signature: Error loading shared library.*task-private runtime|\.codesign count is one.*loader rejects|copied shared ELF.*RC 127
severity: 1
category: task-private-shared-elf-signing
match_keywords: shared library copy, task-private runtime, old codesign, force re-sign, binary-sign-tool, llvm-objcopy, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, SONAME alias, loader RC 127
title: Re-sign task-private OHOS shared-library copies even when an old codesign exists
root_cause: A unique .codesign section proves only structural presence. Copying an already-signed provider ELF or its materialized SONAME aliases into a task-private runtime root changes the execution artifact boundary, and the target loader can reject the copy even when bytes, mode, RPATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH are otherwise correct. An existing-section fast path therefore bypasses the only operation that establishes a current target signature for the private copy.
affected_scope: OpenHarmony package consumers that materialize Conan shared-library closures or SONAME aliases into task-private directories before target execution.
verification_cmd: Copy the complete shared dependency closure without mutating the Conan cache; strip an old .codesign from a sibling temporary input, sign to a second sibling temporary, require exactly one new .codesign and owner execute, atomically replace the private copy, then run the unchanged consumer under the exact private runtime path.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: force-resign-private-runtime-copies
rec_description: Preserve the provider cache as read-only. For every task-private ELF copy, reject duplicate sections and stale temporaries, remove one old .codesign from a private temporary, sign that temporary, verify the signed output, restore owner execute, atomically publish it over the private copy, and clean only invocation-owned temporaries on failure.
rec_command: llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign private.unsigned && binary-sign-tool sign -inFile private.unsigned -outFile private.signed -selfSign 1 && llvm-readelf -SW private.signed
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: preserve-provider-layout-and-fail-closed
fallback_description: If the current target signer or objcopy is unavailable, leave the provider cache and private copy unchanged and report runtime NOT_RUN or failure according to the task contract; do not claim success from section presence alone.
fallback_command: verify tool capability before materialization and stop before consumer execution
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: if existing_codesign == 1.*return|copy2\(.*\.so.*\).*execute
forbid_1_reason: A structural fast path reuses provider signing state without establishing that the task-private copy is accepted by the current target loader.
forbid_1_consequence: The consumer starts but reports missing SONAME libraries and unresolved symbols with RC 127 despite a complete runtime path.
forbid_2_pattern: llvm-objcopy.*Conan cache|binary-sign-tool.*Conan cache
forbid_2_reason: Dependency packages are shared immutable inputs and must not be rewritten for one consumer transaction.
forbid_2_consequence: Cross-task cache corruption and unverifiable provider package identity.
doc_file: doc/E452.md
similar_to: E077
